### 1. Crea l'admin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mail": "admin@unina.it",
  "username": "admin",
  "rawPassword": "Admin01!",
  "repeatRawPassword": "Admin01!",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### 1b. Crea l'user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mail": "Pippo@unina.it",
  "username": "Pippo",
  "rawPassword": "PWperfetta?1",
  "repeatRawPassword": "PWperfetta?1",
  "role": "USER"
}

### 2. Login con admin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mail": "admin@unina.it",
  "rawPassword": "Admin01!"
}

> {% client.global.set("auth_token", response.body.token) %}

### 2b. Login con user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mail": "Pippo@unina.it",
  "rawPassword": "PWperfetta?1"
}

> {% client.global.set("auth_token", response.body.token) %}

### 3. Visualizza users
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 4. Controllo se ho il login
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 5. Crea tag 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Backend"
}

### 5b. Crea tag 2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Frontend"
}

### 5c. Crea tag 3
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Graphics"
}

### 5d. Crea tag 4
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "OutOfBoundsGlitch"
}

### 6. Visualizza tags
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 7. Crea issue 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "MiaIssue1",
  "description": "Risolvete la prima issue",
  "imageName": "Ciaone.txt",
  "rawImage": "DkHwDA==",
  "priority": false,
  "type": "BUG"
}

### 7b. Crea issue 2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mia bella Issue2",
  "description": "Risolvete la seconda issue",
  "priority": true,
  "imageName": "Ciaone",
  "tags": ["Graphics", "Frontend"],
  "type": "FEATURE"
}

### 7c. Crea issue 3
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mia bella Issue3",
  "description": "Risolvete la terza issue",
  "priority": true,
  "imageName": "Ciaone",
  "rawImage": ["12"],
  "tags": ["Backend"],
  "type": "FEATURE"
}

### 7d. Crea issue 4
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mia bella Issue4",
  "description": "Risolvete la quarta issue",
  "priority": true,
  "tags": ["OutOfBoundsGlitch", "Frontend"],
  "type": "BUG"
}

### 8. Assegna issue
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/issues/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "issue": {
    "id": 3
  },
  "user": {
    "id": 1
  }
}

### 9. Visualizza issues
GET http://localhost:8080/api/issues

### 10a. Filtra issue: prendi issue specifica
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1
}

### 10b. Filtra issue: prendi issues segnalate da reportingUser 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reportingUserId": 1
}

### 10c. Filtra issue: prendi issues assegnate da assignedUser 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assignedUserId": 1
}

### 10d. Filtra issue: prendi issues di un certo tipo
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FEATURE"
}

### 10e. Filtra issue: prendi issues di un certo stato
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "INPROGRESS"
}

### 10f. Filtra issue: prendi issues con/senza priorità
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priority": false
}

### 10g. Filtra issue: prendi issues in un certo range di data di creazione
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "startCreationDate": "2026-05-12T14:46:38",
  "endCreationDate": "2026-05-12T14:46:56"
}

### 10h. Filtra issue: prendi issues in un certo range di data di ultima modifica
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "startLastModifiedDate": "2026-05-12T14:47:38",
  "endLastModifiedDate": "2026-05-12T14:51:56"
}


### 10i. Filtra issue: prendi issues con almeno i tag segnati
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tags": ["Frontend"]
}

### 10j. Filtra issue: prendi issue specifica
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "hasImage": false
}

### 10k. Filtra issue: prendi tutte le issue
POST http://localhost:8080/api/issues/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
}

### 11. Chiude issue duplicata
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/issues/close
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "BUG"
}

### 12. Visualizza users per disponibilità
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/available
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 13. Aggiorna stato della issue
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/issues/status
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 3,
  "newStatus": "INPROGRESS"
}

### 14. Visualizza history della prima issue
GET http://localhost:8080/api/issues/history
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1
}